export default {"groups":[{"title":"Source and compulsory release","keys":["routing","limits","special","sourcepowers"]},{"title":"Privacy and data transfer","keys":["ipp","hpp","healthspecial","transfers"]},{"title":"Statutory information sharing","keys":["vds","vdsdetail","ciss","fviss","schemeproof"]},{"title":"FOI, public access, and reporting","keys":["foi","foiadmin","foiex","reporting"]},{"title":"Government policy and decision","keys":["policy","controls","record","csa"]}],"labels":{"routing":"intake and classification","limits":"source restrictions","special":"restricted records and legal demands","sourcepowers":"housing and care clauses","ipp":"IPP 2","hpp":"HPP 2","healthspecial":"specialist health tests","transfers":"transfer and recipient checks","vds":"Victorian Data Sharing Act","vdsdetail":"CDO refusal and secrecy tests","ciss":"CISS","fviss":"FVISS","schemeproof":"scheme eligibility and records","foi":"FOI and publication","foiadmin":"FOI intake and decision","foiex":"FOI exemption tests","reporting":"corporate disclosure","policy":"government data policy","controls":"final release checks","record":"decision record","csa":"CSA example","home":"Start"},"pages":{"routing":{"category":"START HERE","title":"Identify the request and the decision","intro":"Record the exact information, source program, legal recipient and capacity, purpose, destination, intended audience, and proposed onward use.","rows":[["I1","Immediate harm or a statutory clock","Is there an immediate safety risk, a court return date, a valid FOI request, or a formal statutory or policy notice? Record when it arrived and the due date.","Activate the applicable urgent response in parallel with the release test. Use [limits], [foi], [vds], [ciss], [fviss], or [policy].","Use I2."],["I2","What is being requested?","Is an individual seeking adoption or care history, or is a subpoena, warrant, oversight demand, or protected disclosure involved?","Use [special] for the dedicated route. Escalate a binding instrument promptly.","Use I3."],["I3","Classify information field by field","Does it identify a living individual or can their identity reasonably be worked out in context? Does it concern health, disability, a health service, or another category in the HRA definition, including qualifying information about a deceased person?","Use [ipp] for non-health personal information and [hpp] for health information. For mixed releases assess both. Check source rules for every field.","Assess source limits even for non-identifying data. Demonstrate lawful departmental function and use [controls]."],["I4","Purpose and legal capacity","Can you name the departmental function or specific power, the legal entity receiving the data, and why it needs this version? For onward sharing, is the proposed recipient and further purpose within the original conditions?","Select the applicable authority and [policy]. A single extract can have more than one source restriction.","Pause and obtain the missing facts. If the function or authority remains unestablished, use [record]."],["I5","Public release is its own decision","Will the material be available to an unrestricted audience, including through a dashboard, media release, data portal, or access link?","Use the public release branches of [foi] and [policy]. Test reasonable identification against data available publicly.","Assess the named recipient, role, controlled access, and onward disclosure separately."]],"note":"Obtain evidence of the proposed facts and authority. A missing fact is a hold or escalation outcome. If a deadline or safety duty applies, send the matter to the appropriate decision-maker promptly.","sources":[["Privacy Act definitions","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/privacy-and-data-protection-act-2014/034"],["Health Records Act definitions","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/health-records-act-2001/050"],["OVIC information sharing","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/privacy/resources-for-organisations/information-sharing-and-privacy/"]],"number":2},"limits":{"number":3,"category":"SOURCE AND COMPULSION","title":"What governs the source records?","intro":"Apply the restriction checks to the precise fields or words being released. Use the source program’s actual legislation, orders, instruments, and terms.","rows":[["S1","Binding disclosure","Does a verified provision, order, subpoena, or notice <b>require DFFH</b> to disclose this material to this recipient? Check scope, privilege, deadline, and any conflict with secrecy.","<b>Must disclose</b> to the extent required, once the scope and any conflicts are resolved. Apply the instrument’s handling rules and [controls].","Use S2. Test [ciss], [fviss], or [vds] for a scheme duty."],["S2","Restriction or confidentiality","Is the proposed version restricted by secrecy, a statutory use limit, court order, privilege, confidentiality, or binding terms? Check each contributing dataset.","Test the exact exception or override. If none applies, withhold or lawfully redact and retest. For Child Protection see S3–S4. Use [special] for other restrictions.","Continue with the applicable pathway. Use [special] for an adoption or care history request."],["S3","CYFA ss 41, 190–191","Would a Child Protection or child-and-family-services record reveal a protected reporter or referrer, including indirectly? Identify the report or referral and the exact provision that applies.","Confirm a specific exception, e.g. written consent or a permitted recipient. For evidence check s 190 and any required leave. Otherwise withhold details likely to identify the person.","Continue with S4. Check the Child Protection Manual for other confidential sources, including investigation sources."],["S4","CYFA ss 179, 192","Does s 179(1) or (2) apply to a prospective or actual carer? Otherwise, does the Secretary or a protective intervener reasonably believe disclosure is required for a CYFA duty, function, or power, and is the recipient within s 192(1)(a)–(f)?","Use [sourcepowers] for the exact conditions and scope, then [controls].","Use another lawful pathway, such as CISS or FVISS, if its conditions are met."],["S5","Youth Justice Act ss 704(2), 705, 708","Is Child Protection or an authorised Aboriginal community-controlled organisation sharing with Youth Justice where reasonably necessary for official functions, or with another qualifying information holder for the purposes in s 708?","Confirm the actor, recipient, and necessity under the exact subsection and Part 15.1. Apply S2 and [controls].","Do not use this authority. Continue via [home]."],["S6","Social Services Regulation Act ss 189, 193(2)","Is the discloser a relevant agency and reasonably satisfied the information is reasonably required for a function conferred on the Regulator under an Act, or that disclosure is necessary to determine whether further information can lawfully be disclosed?","<b>May disclose</b> to the Regulator under s 193(2), subject to Part 8, including any s 201 confidentiality notice. Check s 195 for the separate duty to assist. Apply [controls].","Check another Part 8 authority or use another pathway."],["S7","Housing Act ss 142G–142J","Is disclosure between relevant persons under s 142I and necessary for a listed s 142J(1) purpose? For establishing, administering, or maintaining the register, check the discloser’s authorisation and s 142J(2).","Apply purpose and recipient tests in [sourcepowers], then [controls].","Use another applicable authority."]],"note":"Check other source-specific regimes where they apply. For linked, Commonwealth-supplied, or third-party data, verify the terms and legislation attached to each input.","sources":[["CYFA","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/children-youth-and-families-act-2005/149"],["DFFH Child Protection Manual","https://www.cpmanual.vic.gov.au/our-approach/information-sharing/information-sharing-child-protection-practice"],["Youth Justice Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/youth-justice-act-2024"],["Social Services Regulation Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/social-services-regulation-act-2021/009"],["Housing Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/housing-act-1983"]]},"special":{"category":"SOURCE-SPECIFIC AND COMPULSORY PATHWAYS","title":"Handle restricted records and legal demands","intro":"Use this branch with the [limits] branch. If a limit applies, withhold the affected material unless a verified exception, override, or duty applies.","rows":[["S8","CYFA s 534 • public identification","Would publication reveal, or be likely to reveal, that a child is or was the subject of a relevant Children’s Court proceeding or protection order, or identify another protected participant in connection with the proceeding?","Hold the public version. Remove identifying connections and retest, or obtain any required permission from the President of the Children’s Court before publication.","Continue other restrictions and the public-release tests."],["S9","Adoption Act 1984 • Part VI","Is the request for an adoption order, birth record, or identifying adoption information? Is the applicant the adopted person, a natural parent or relative, an adoptive parent, or another person?","Refer to Adoption Information Service. It verifies identity, applicant category, age, consent and restrictions. Other non-relatives generally apply to County Court under s 100. Keep records pending an authorised decision.","For care history consider S10."],["S10","DFFH Care Leavers Access to Records Policy","Is a person seeking their own DFFH out-of-home care records? Have identity or representative authority been verified?","Use the dedicated care records process. Screen reporter/referrer identity and sensitive third-party material, and consult where practicable. Provide approved material by that process.","Clarify identity or go to [foi] for other requests."],["S11","Court or oversight instrument","Has Legal or the statutory liaison confirmed the issuer’s power, service, addressee, material and deadline, and resolved privilege, immunity, secrecy, or scope objections? Is the instrument still operative?","Provide the verified required material through the designated channel. Preserve any claim, return instructions, and limits on access or publication.","Hold voluntary transmission. Refer promptly for a decision on validity, objections, and urgent compliance."],["S12","Special evidence, agreements, or protected disclosures","Is the material covered by an actual suppression order, source agreement, restricted Commonwealth dataset, protected disclosure, or a program-specific confidentiality duty beyond the mapped routes?","Record the instrument, clause, scope, and accountable owner. For protected disclosures refer to the designated coordinator. Where the instrument remains unclear, use the referral outcome on [record].","Proceed through the applicable release pathway."]],"note":"A subpoena or oversight notice is assessed against its own terms. An order permitting access to a document may still limit use or public release. Record the restriction and decision separately.","sources":[["CYFA","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/children-youth-and-families-act-2005/149"],["Adoption Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/adoption-act-1984"],["Care Leavers policy","https://www.dffh.vic.gov.au/sites/default/files/documents/202110/Care%20Leavers%20Access%20to%20Records%20Policy.pdf"],["Open Courts Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/open-courts-act-2013"],["Public Interest Disclosures Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/public-interest-disclosures-act-2012"]],"number":4},"sourcepowers":{"category":"SOURCE AUTHORITY • CLAUSE CONDITIONS","title":"Decide housing and care disclosures","intro":"Use these tests for the specific permissions in [limits]. Recipient identity and the purpose of the individual disclosure must be established.","rows":[["SH1","Housing Act ss 142I–142J(1)","Is the material an applicant or household member’s details, other tenancy-application information, or information about adequacy of housing or future housing needs? Are both parties within the defined relevant persons, such as Homes Victoria, a registered agency, or a designated service provider, including their applicable personnel?","Test the purpose in SH2 and continued source restrictions.","Withhold under this specific route. Establish a different lawful basis or use [record]."],["SH2","Housing Act s 142J(1)(a)–(h)","Is disclosure necessary to assess eligibility or priority, allocate social housing, assess safety, health, support or housing needs, facilitate tenancy management or granting appropriate housing, report or compile statistics on register use, exercise a Housing Act function or power, or give information the Act expressly authorises, permits or requires?","May disclose to the qualifying recipient within the necessary scope. Preserve any restriction under s 142J(3). If administering or correcting the register use SH3.","This specific route does not authorise the proposed disclosure."],["SH3","Housing Act ss 142G–142J(2)","Is the discloser a relevant person with formal access authorisation, and is disclosure to another relevant person necessary to establish or administer the register or maintain its accuracy? For the separate register-access decision, is access by Homes Victoria or an authorised person for the permitted accuracy, eligibility, priority, allocation, verification, reporting, or statutory purposes?","Allow the qualifying access or disclosure within those limits. Apply [controls].","Decline unauthorised access. Establish another applicable authority where relevant."],["SH4","CYFA s 179(1)–(2)","Is Child Protection intending to place a child with someone other than their parent, or has it already placed the child in such a person’s care?","For intended placement, provide information reasonably necessary for an informed choice about accepting care. After placement, provide known information about the child’s medical status so the carer can provide appropriate care.","Check CYFA s 192 and other applicable routes on [limits]."],["SH5","CYFA s 192(1)–(2)","Is the Secretary or a protective intervener disclosing for the statutory duties, functions or powers under s 192(1), on reasonable grounds? Alternatively, is this a response to their request under s 192(2)?","May disclose only within that power. Apply reporter restrictions and [controls].","Use another scheme or withhold pending a lawful authority."]],"note":"Where the eligibility of an actor or recipient turns on its designation, delegation, or service arrangement, obtain evidence from the accountable program before authorising release.","sources":[["Housing Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/housing-act-1983"],["CYFA","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/children-youth-and-families-act-2005/149"],["Child Protection Manual","https://www.cpmanual.vic.gov.au/our-approach/information-sharing/information-sharing-child-protection-practice"]],"number":5},"ipp":{"number":6,"category":"ORDINARY PRIVACY PATHWAY","title":"Personal information under IPP 2","intro":"Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014 (Vic), Schedule 1. Test the primary purpose first, then the applicable secondary-purpose grounds. Each secondary ground is an alternative.","rows":[["P1","IPP 2.1 • primary purpose","Is the proposed disclosure for the actual primary purpose for which DFFH collected the information?","Privacy ground met. Go to [controls].","Test P2–P9 for an applicable ground."],["P2","IPP 2.1(a)(i)–(ii)","Is the secondary purpose related to the primary purpose (directly related for sensitive information), <b>and</b> would the person reasonably expect this disclosure for that purpose?","Record the link and evidence of reasonable expectation. Go to [controls].","Test another secondary ground."],["P3","IPP 2.1(b)","Has the person validly consented to this specific disclosure? Confirm capacity, informed and voluntary consent, its current scope, and any withdrawal.","Use the consent’s scope and conditions. Go to [controls].","Test another secondary ground."],["P4","IPP 2.1(c)(i)–(ii)","Is disclosure necessary for public-interest research or statistics, with no identifying publication? Is seeking consent impracticable? Does DFFH reasonably believe the recipient will keep the information from onward disclosure?","Record necessity, public interest, consent impracticability, and the basis for that belief. Go to [controls].","Test a different ground or reassess a lawfully de-identified version."],["P5","IPP 2.1(d)(i)–(ii)","Does DFFH reasonably believe disclosure is necessary to lessen or prevent a serious threat to a person’s life, health, safety, or welfare, or to public health, safety, or welfare?","Limit the disclosure to addressing the threat. Go to [controls].","Test another secondary ground."],["P6","IPP 2.1(e)","Does DFFH have reason to suspect past, present, or possible unlawful activity, with disclosure necessary to investigate or report that concern to relevant people or authorities?","Record the suspicion, necessity, and recipient. Go to [controls].","Test another secondary ground."],["P7","IPP 2.1(f)","Does a specific law require or authorise DFFH’s disclosure, and are its conditions met for this purpose, recipient, and information?","Use that law’s scope and decision type. Go to [controls].","Test another secondary ground."],["P8","IPP 2.1(g)(i)–(v), IPP 2.2","Does DFFH reasonably believe disclosure is reasonably necessary for an enumerated purpose by or for a law enforcement agency? Match the exact limb: offences or sanctions, proceeds of crime, public revenue, serious misconduct, or court/tribunal proceedings or orders.","Make the written record required by IPP 2.2. Go to [controls].","Test another secondary ground."],["P9","IPP 2.1(h)(i)–(ii)","Is this a function-related request from ASIO or ASIS, with an authorised recipient and a certificate from an officer or employee authorised in writing for that purpose?","Verify the written authorisations and certificate. Go to [controls].","If no privacy ground applies, withhold this version or redesign and retest."]],"note":"For a mixed release, test the health information and personal information under the applicable regimes. Check IPP 7.3 for unique identifiers assigned by another organisation, and IPP 9.1 for transfers outside Victoria.","sources":[["PDP Act, Schedule 1","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/privacy-and-data-protection-act-2014/034"],["OVIC IPP 2 guide","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/privacy/resources-for-organisations/information-privacy-principle-2-pocket-guide/"],["OVIC sharing guidance","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/privacy/resources-for-organisations/information-sharing-and-privacy/"]]},"hpp":{"number":7,"category":"HEALTH PRIVACY PATHWAY","title":"Health information under HPP 2","intro":"Health Records Act 2001 (Vic), s 3 and Schedule 1. Health information may appear in a housing or casework record. Test the content and the purpose of release.","rows":[["H1","HPP 2.1, 2.2(a)–(c)","Is it the primary purpose of lawful collection, a directly related secondary purpose the person would reasonably expect, valid consent, or a disclosure required, authorised, or permitted by law other than a prescribed law?","Record the exact ground and any limits. Go to [controls].","Test H2–H7 for an applicable ground."],["H2","HPP 2.2(f)(i)–(vi)","Is the purpose specified health-service funding, management, planning, monitoring, improvement, evaluation, or qualifying provider training? Either de-identified data cannot serve it and consent is impracticable, <b>or</b> reasonable de-identification steps are taken. Are any s 22 guidelines followed and any reasonably identifying material kept out of generally available publications?","Record which limb and safeguards apply. Go to [controls].","Test another health ground."],["H3","HPP 2.2(g)(i)–(iv)","Is disclosure necessary for public-interest research or statistics? Is seeking consent impracticable, is de-identified information insufficient, and are s 22 research guidelines met? Does DFFH reasonably believe the recipient will keep the health information from onward disclosure, and will publication avoid identifying anyone?","Record the evidence for each element, including applicable ethics review under the guidelines. Go to [controls].","Test another ground or reassess a lawfully de-identified version."],["H4","HPP 2.2(h)","Does DFFH reasonably believe disclosure is necessary to lessen or prevent a serious threat to a person’s life, health, safety, or welfare, or to public health, safety, or welfare? Are any applicable s 22 guidelines met?","Limit the disclosure to addressing the threat. Go to [controls].","Test another health ground."],["H5","HPP 2.2(i)–(j), HPP 2.3","Is disclosure necessary to investigate or report suspected unlawful activity, or does DFFH reasonably believe disclosure is reasonably necessary for a law enforcement function by or for a law enforcement agency? For a registered practitioner, would it preserve confidence?","Make the written note required by HPP 2.3. Go to [controls].","Test another health ground."],["H6","HPP 2.2(k)–(l)","Is disclosure necessary to establish, exercise, or defend a legal or equitable claim, or does it fall within circumstances prescribed under the Act?","Confirm the claim or current prescription and scope. Go to [controls].","Test H7 if relevant."],["H7","HPP 2.2(d), 2.4, 2.5","Is this a specialist disclosure, e.g. providing care to a person unable to consent, disclosure by a provider to immediate family, or identifying or locating someone in specified situations? Check each condition, including s 85 where applicable. HPP 2.2(e) addresses use for further health services by the provider.","Apply the precise tests in [healthspecial] before [controls].","If no health privacy ground applies, withhold this version or redesign and retest."]],"note":"Where another enactment is relied on, identify the precise power and recipient. Check HPP 7 for identifiers and HPP 9 for transborder transfers. A health privacy permission does not create a duty to disclose.","sources":[["Health Records Act, Schedule 1","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/health-records-act-2001/050"],["HCC statutory research guidelines","https://hcc.vic.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-04/guidelines_research_vic_gazette.pdf"]]},"healthspecial":{"category":"HEALTH PRIVACY • SPECIAL CASES","title":"Decide the specialist health disclosures","intro":"Use this branch for the exceptions referred to in H7. A permission is limited to the situation and recipient described in the applicable provision.","rows":[["HS1","HPP 2.2(d) and HRA s 85","Is the discloser a health service provider delivering the service to the individual? Is disclosure reasonably necessary for that service? Is the individual incapable of consenting, and either has no authorised representative or it is not reasonably practicable to obtain that representative’s consent?","<b>May disclose</b> to the extent reasonably necessary for the health service. Confirm incapacity and any representative before [controls].","Use HS2 or HS3 if relevant, or another [hpp] ground."],["HS2","HPP 2.4 • immediate family","Is the discloser a provider, the recipient immediate family, and the individual incapable of consenting? Is disclosure needed for care, or compassionate, and limited to what is reasonable and necessary? Does it respect discoverable prior wishes, and is any recipient under 18 sufficiently mature in the circumstances?","<b>May disclose</b> to the immediate family member within those limits. Go to [controls].","Withhold under this route. Consider other health grounds."],["HS3","HPP 2.5 • missing, death, or accident","Is the individual known or suspected to be dead or missing, or involved in an accident or misadventure and incapable of consenting? Is the proposed disclosure reasonably necessary to identify them or locate an eligible relative to help identify the person or enable police, a coroner, or a prescribed organisation to contact the relative compassionately?","In missing or accident cases, check reasonably discoverable prior wishes. Follow any applicable HCC guidelines. If these conditions pass, <b>may disclose</b> within scope.","Use another [hpp] ground or hold."],["HS4","HPP 2.2(e) • further services","Is the provider proposing internal use to safely and effectively deliver its own further health services to the person under HPP 2.2(e)?","Confine that decision to the qualifying internal use, including any applicable guidelines. Assess any actual disclosure under a separate ground.","Use the relevant [hpp] disclosure ground."],["HS5","HPP 2.2(g) • research practice","For the research route, has DFFH identified how it will meet the HCC statutory research guidelines, including relevant ethics committee approval and specified safeguards for identifiable research or statistics?","Confirm approval and conditions alongside all H3 requirements. Record the minimum disclosure, secure recipient, and publication constraints.","Hold the identifiable research release. Consider a lawful non-identifying version or another verified pathway."]],"note":"Consent and representative powers can differ by person and context. Record the basis of the decision and what the representative can authorise before relying on their consent.","sources":[["Health Records Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/health-records-act-2001/050"],["HCC statutory research guidelines","https://hcc.vic.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-04/guidelines_research_vic_gazette.pdf"]],"number":8},"vds":{"number":9,"category":"GOVERNMENT ANALYTICS PATHWAY","title":"Victorian Data Sharing Act 2017","intro":"Check the requester, purpose, and legal recipient. A Chief Data Officer request can cover non-identifying data. Direct disclosure under s 15(2) concerns identifiable data for integration with an eligible data analytics body.","rows":[["V1","ss 3, 5 and 8(3)","Is the data handled to inform government policy making, service planning, or design? Have the relevant entities and data been classified under s 3? The CDO cannot request restricted data under s 8(3).","Check V2 for a CDO request or V3 for direct integration.","Use another applicable pathway. Do not supply restricted data in response to a purported s 8 request."],["V2","ss 8(1)–(2), 9, 14, 15(1)","Is there a written CDO notice to the responsible officer identifying the requested data, reasons, and proposed handling? Is DFFH a data sharing body for this request?","Respond within 10 business days or an agreed longer period. Use [vdsdetail] to decide partial or full refusal and secrecy.","Check V3 for direct integration, or [policy] if the request came from an eligible agency under the VPS policy."],["V3","ss 3, 5, 15(2)","Will the responsible officer disclose identifiable data to a qualifying data analytics body specifically for data integration? Verify whether the recipient is a department Secretary or a body or person prescribed under s 3.","<b>May disclose</b> within s 15(2) if restrictions permit. Verify the legal recipient and delegation. Check V4–V5 before [controls].","Use another sharing basis."],["V4","ss 20–23","Does a secrecy provision apply to the proposed data? Identify the provision, any preservation by regulation, and whether the disclosure is to the CDO under this Act.","Follow [vdsdetail] for refusals, secrecy notice and authorisations.","Use V5 for integration, analytics, or outcomes."],["V5","ss 16–19, 24","Has the receiving CDO or analytics body confined identifiable data to the applicable integration route, taken reasonable steps to de-identify before analytics, and ensured proposed analytics results contain only de-identified data before disclosure?","Apply [controls]. Record the applicable s 24 privacy obligations and assess any later release separately.","Hold the analytics use or output release. Correct the scope or de-identification and retest."],["V6","s 25(1)(a)–(b)","Is a formal FOI request for a document in the CDO’s or an analytics body’s possession containing one of the listed supplied-data, data-holdings, or integration products?","Refer to FOI for the s 25 scope decision. Consider whether the source agency holds an accessible original.","Use [foi] to test other exclusions and exemptions."]],"note":"Non-identifying data does not by itself exclude the Act. Section 5 concerns policy making, service planning, and design. Operational service delivery is a different purpose. Ordinary interagency requests may instead use an established agency function and the separate VPS policy. Confirm the exact legal basis before release.","sources":[["Victorian Data Sharing Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/victorian-data-sharing-act-2017/002"],["VPS Data Sharing Policy","https://www.vic.gov.au/victorian-public-sector-data-sharing-policy"],["Government data sharing guidance","https://www.vic.gov.au/navigating-legislation-sharing-safely"]]},"vdsdetail":{"category":"VICTORIAN DATA SHARING ACT • REQUESTS AND SECRECY","title":"Check refusal grounds and onward disclosure","intro":"Start on the Victorian Data Sharing Act page. Use these conditions where the route involves a Chief Data Officer request, secrecy, or a downstream analytics disclosure.","rows":[["VD1","VDS Act ss 3, 8(3)","Could the data expose an enforcement confidential source, a protected witness, or law enforcement investigative measures or procedures, or prejudice national security?","Hold under a Chief Data Officer s 8 request. The restricted-data bar applies. Escalate uncertain classifications.","Apply V2 and VD2."],["VD2","VDS Act ss 9, 14","Does the responsible officer consider some or all should be withheld? Possible reasons include privilege, contract, equitable confidence, court or tribunal order, other applicable law, likely prejudice to enforcement, an inquest or proceeding, or reasonably grounded likely danger to health, safety or welfare.","Within the s 9 period give written reasons to the CDO and the Secretary identified by s 9(3). Provide any approved remainder.","Provide approved data within 10 business days or an agreed longer period. For secrecy use VD3."],["VD3","VDS Act ss 20–21","Is secrecy-protected data being supplied by the responsible officer to the CDO in accordance with and for the purposes of the Act? Does the officer know a secrecy provision applies?","If that route applies, give the required notice of the secrecy provision as soon as practicable. Document its identity and limits.","Resolve the secrecy restriction before sharing. Section 20 applies to the CDO route."],["VD4","VDS Act ss 16, 23","Does the CDO propose to share data to which secrecy applies? Has the responsible Minister authorised disclosure, and for Taxation Administration Act secrecy has the Commissioner of State Revenue also authorised it? For identifiable data, is the eligible body receiving it for integration under s 16?","If every condition applies, may disclose under the CDO process and its conditions.","Hold the proposed onward disclosure."],["VD5","VDS Act ss 18–19, 25","Will the recipient use data for analytics or publish the results? Have reasonable de-identification steps been completed before use in analytics, and do the proposed results contain only de-identified data?","Record the applied techniques and safeguards. Treat FOI requests for enumerated documents held by the CDO or analytics body under the special s 25 route.","Hold the analytics use or result release until the applicable standard is met."]],"note":"The statutory response route under the Act concerns the Chief Data Officer. For an eligible request by another Victorian agency under government policy, use the separate policy branch.","sources":[["Victorian Data Sharing Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/victorian-data-sharing-act-2017/002"],["Government data policy","https://www.vic.gov.au/victorian-public-sector-data-sharing-policy"]],"number":10},"ciss":{"number":11,"category":"CHILD WELLBEING AND SAFETY PATHWAY","title":"Child Information Sharing Scheme","intro":"Child Wellbeing and Safety Act 2005 (Vic), Part 6A. Apply C1–C3 to sharing between entities. Use C5 for a proposed disclosure directly to a child or caregiver.","rows":[["C1","ss 41P, 41R–41T and regulations","Are the disclosing and receiving entities prescribed in the relevant capacity? Is the information confidential within s 41P? Check any restriction on entity class or function, including courts and tribunals.","Use [schemeproof] to confirm capacity, then C2 and C3.","Check C5 if the recipient is a child or caregiver. Otherwise use another pathway."],["C2","s 41Q • excluded information","Would disclosure reasonably be expected to put life or physical safety at risk, prejudice law enforcement, an inquest or a fair hearing, reveal privileged material or a confidential enforcement source, contravene relevant orders or closed-proceedings provisions, or be contrary to the public interest? Is the information prescribed as excluded?","Withhold the excluded portion under this scheme. Check the DFFH source laws, including reporter identity protections, at [limits].","Test C3 (or C5 for direct disclosure)."],["C3","ss 41V(a)–(b), 41W(3)(a)–(b)","Is the disclosure for promoting the wellbeing or safety of a child or group? Does DFFH reasonably believe sharing may help the recipient make a decision, assessment or plan, investigate, provide a service, or manage a risk for the child or group?","Test C4 to distinguish a request from voluntary sharing.","This scheme does not authorise this proposed release. If refusing a valid s 41W(1) request, give written reasons under s 41W(4), subject to s 41W(5)."],["C4","ss 41V, 41W(1), (3)–(5)","Is this a valid s 41W(1) request from an eligible entity, meeting C1–C3, with no s 41W(5) exception?","<b>Must disclose</b> the qualifying portion. If part is withheld, record and give the applicable written reasons. Go to C6.","If initiated by DFFH and C1–C3 are met, <b>may disclose</b> under s 41V. Otherwise check the request or another pathway."],["C5","s 41Y(1)–(2)","Is DFFH a prescribed entity, is the material free of excluded information, and is disclosure to the child, a person with parental responsibility, or the person the child lives with, to manage a risk to the child’s safety?","<b>May disclose</b> for managing that risk. The recipient’s use or disclosure is limited to that purpose. Go to C6.","Use another applicable pathway."],["C6","ss 41U, 41ZA, 41ZC","Have you applied the statutory principles, Ministerial Guidelines, and prescribed records? Consider child and family views where safe, appropriate, and reasonable, and share only the information needed.","Apply [schemeproof] and [controls], then disclose within the applicable permission or duty.","Resolve missing safeguards or record requirements promptly. Escalate any urgent safety issue through the appropriate process."]],"note":"Consent is not a condition of release under the CISS provisions above. Follow the statutory principles and guidance on seeking and considering views, as well as the requirements for documenting the decision.","sources":[["CWS Act, Part 6A","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/child-wellbeing-and-safety-act-2005/048"],["CISS regulations","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/statutory-rules/child-wellbeing-and-safety-information-sharing-regulations-2018"],["Ministerial Guidelines","https://www.vic.gov.au/child-information-sharing-scheme-ministerial-guidelines"]]},"fviss":{"number":12,"category":"FAMILY VIOLENCE PATHWAY","title":"Family Violence Information Sharing Scheme","intro":"Family Violence Protection Act 2008 (Vic), Part 5A. Choose assessment (establish risk) or protection (manage risk, including ongoing assessment).","rows":[["F1","ss 144A–144D, 144K, 144L","Are DFFH and the recipient prescribed in the relevant capacities and is the information within the categories for the selected purpose? For assessment, the recipient must be a risk assessment entity. For protection, it must be a qualifying information sharing entity.","Use [schemeproof] to confirm eligibility. Then test F2 and F3.","Check F5 for direct disclosure to a primary person, or another pathway."],["F2","s 144C • excluded information","Is the information prescribed as excluded, or could sharing reasonably be expected to endanger life, cause physical injury, prejudice an investigation/enforcement, inquest, or fair hearing, reveal privileged material or a confidential enforcement source, contravene specified orders or proceeding restrictions, or be contrary to the public interest?","Withhold the excluded portion under this scheme. Check other source restrictions at [limits].","Test F3."],["F3","ss 144N–144ND • consent","Is the information about a person of concern or alleged risk (s 144N), a child primary person for a s 144NC(1) purpose, or an adult/linked person whose information relates to that qualifying child information (s 144NC(2))? Otherwise, does the adult primary or linked person consent, or does DFFH reasonably believe sharing is necessary to lessen or prevent a serious threat to a person’s life, health, safety, or welfare?","Record the exact consent rule, capacity if relevant, and how it is met. Go to F4.","Do not disclose these fields under this scheme. For a request, apply the relevant written-reasons rule."],["F4","ss 144KA–KC, 144LA–LC","Has the qualifying entity requested the information for an eligible purpose? For protection requests, does DFFH reasonably believe disclosure is necessary for that purpose? Check the exclusions, consent rules, and the s 144KC(2) / s 144LC(2) court/body exceptions.","<b>Must disclose</b> qualifying material under s 144KC or s 144LC. Go to F6.","For non-compliance give written reasons under s 144KB(3) or s 144LB(3). If voluntary and eligible, <b>may disclose</b> under s 144KA or s 144LA."],["F5","ss 144M–144MA • direct disclosure","Is DFFH disclosing non-excluded information about a person of concern to a primary person for protection under s 144M(1), or to the child primary person or their parent who is not a person of concern in relation to the child under s 144M(2)?","<b>May disclose</b>. Recipient use and disclosure are limited by s 144MA to managing the primary person’s risk. Go to F6.","Check another applicable pathway."],["F6","ss 144J, 144P, 144PB","Have you applied the principles, binding guidelines where applicable, and prescribed recordkeeping requirements? Have you considered relevant child and adult safety, disclosure scope, and safe handling?","Apply [schemeproof] and [controls], then disclose within the applicable permission or duty.","Resolve missing safeguards or record requirements promptly. Escalate urgent risk through the appropriate process."]],"note":"Check s 144QA separately if access to a person’s own information could increase a primary person’s family violence risk. Section 144Q preserves other lawful pathways.","sources":[["FVPA, Part 5A","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/family-violence-protection-act-2008/071"],["FVISS regulations","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/statutory-rules/family-violence-protection-information-sharing-and-risk-management"],["Victorian Government FVISS guidance","https://www.vic.gov.au/overview-family-violence-information-sharing-scheme-0"]]},"schemeproof":{"category":"CHILD AND FAMILY VIOLENCE SCHEMES","title":"Check eligibility, secrecy, and records","intro":"Use these tests with the CISS and FVISS decision branches. Confirm the actual entity and its function, including the capacity in which it requests or discloses information.","rows":[["SP1","CISS regs 5, 5A–5C, Schedule 1","Is each party confirmed for its role as a prescribed information sharing entity? Is the actor authorised to use that power? A restricted information sharing entity operates within its specific statutory role. A prescription for one service or function does not cover unrelated functions.","Record the legal entity, prescribed capacity, and authorised contact. Return to [ciss].","Verify using the department’s entity register or Information Sharing team. Hold under this scheme until confirmed."],["SP2","FVISS regs 5–8, Schedules 1–2","Is each party a prescribed information sharing entity, and is an assessment recipient also a prescribed risk assessment entity? Has the relevant delegation been confirmed? For Central Information Point use, confirm its specific statutory role and the requester or custodian role.","Record the capacities and apply [fviss]. Refer Central Information Point activity to its authorised workflow.","Hold under this route pending verification. Use another established authority if applicable."],["SP3","CISS s 41ZH, reg 10","Does a currently applicable CISS regulation expressly prescribe the exact secrecy provision as one displaced by s 41ZH? Check the current instrument and any transitional treatment of renamed or repealed laws.","Where that exact provision applies, s 41ZH allows sharing in accordance with Part 6A despite it. Apply the remaining CISS conditions. Refer unresolved legacy-law or other conflicts.","Apply other source limits. For a protected identity or order, use [limits] and [special]."],["SP4","FVISS s 144QC(b), reg 15","Does a currently applicable FVISS regulation expressly prescribe the exact secrecy provision for s 144QC(b)? Verify the current provision and any relevant transitional treatment. Support and Safety Hub and Central Information Point roles require their specific workflows.","Part 5A sharing may proceed despite the prescribed provision if the other tests are met. A Support and Safety Hub has a separate, role-specific process.","Apply other source limits. Do not treat the scheme as a general override."],["SP5","CISS regs 6–9 and FVISS regs 9–14","Have you recorded the request and disclosure dates, entities, what was shared, and required risk assessment or safety plan records, where applicable? Record relevant views, notice, consent or the reason for proceeding without it, and the reason for any refusal.","Preserve the scheme record and any complaint and response. Use the applicable release or written reasons step.","Complete or correct the record promptly through the authorised workflow."]],"note":"Entity prescription and authority are factual checks. If the recipient’s specific function cannot be verified, the decision is to hold or refer, rather than infer eligibility from the organisation name.","sources":[["CISS regulations","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/statutory-rules/child-wellbeing-and-safety-information-sharing-regulations-2018"],["FVISS regulations","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/statutory-rules/family-violence-protection-information-sharing-and-risk-management"],["Victorian scheme entity guidance","https://www.vic.gov.au/ciss-and-fviss-who-can-share-information"]],"number":13},"foi":{"number":14,"category":"ACCESS AND PUBLICATION PATHWAY","title":"Formal FOI, informal access, and publication","intro":"Freedom of Information Act 1982 (Vic). Formal access decisions go to the authorised FOI decision-maker. The publication branch starts at A7.","rows":[["A1","ss 13, 17, 19–21, 26","Is this a valid FOI request for agency documents, and is access within the Act? Consider any obligation to assist or transfer, whether s 19 requires a computable document, and statutory decision time and authority.","Apply the request and decision tests at [foiadmin].","Assist the applicant or consider A7 if they seek informal access."],["A2","FOI applicability • VDS Act s 25","Does a statutory exclusion apply to the document or holder, such as the VDS Act s 25 specified documents held by the CDO or a data analytics body?","Apply the exclusion to the affected documents. Check whether an original can be sought from the source agency.","Use A3–A5 and [foiex] to test all relevant exemptions."],["A3","s 33(1)–(4), (9)","Would release unreasonably disclose personal affairs information of any person? Consider identity, address, location, and reasonably identifying information, the circumstances and safety risks, own-information provisions, and consultation requirements and exceptions.","Apply FX4 and FA5. Address any third-party notice and review-related delay before granting access.","Check other exemptions."],["A4","s 38 • secrecy","Does an in-force enactment specifically apply to this kind of information and prohibit the relevant persons from disclosing it? Identify the exact provision and any exception or qualification, such as CYFA reporter protection.","Apply s 38 where the test is met. Check A6 and any separate legal prohibition on actual release.","Check other exemptions."],["A5","FOI Part IV, ss 28–38","Which exemptions apply to the document or part? Test every relevant exemption against the facts using [foiex].","Record the precise provision and follow FA5 for consultation, edited access, notices, and review.","If no exemption or other ground applies, grant access in accordance with s 13."],["A6","ss 25, 27","Can exempt or irrelevant information practicably be removed, and does the request indicate, or has the applicant said, they would want an edited copy?","<b>Must provide</b> the edited copy under s 25, with the required decision and review information. Clear any third-party release delay first.","Decide access to the remaining documents and give the required notices and review rights."],["A7","s 16(1)–(2) • proactive or informal","Can DFFH properly make this exact version available to this requester or to the public, or does the law require publication? Check any specific publication duty (e.g. s 7), plus source restrictions, privacy, re-identification risk, and licensing.","Apply [policy], [reporting], and [controls] as relevant.","Withhold or redesign the proposed release. For individual access, consider the applicable formal pathway."]],"note":"FOI access is a decision about the applicant’s request. A separate proposal to publish the same material to everyone must be assessed for that audience.","sources":[["FOI Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/freedom-information-act-1982/115"],["OVIC s 16","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-16/"],["OVIC s 25","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-25/"],["OVIC s 33","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-33/"],["OVIC s 38","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-38/"],["DataVic policy","https://www.data.vic.gov.au/datavic-access-policy"]]},"foiadmin":{"category":"FORMAL FOI • INTAKE AND DECISION","title":"Process the request and set the deadline","intro":"Use this section for requests made under the Victorian FOI Act. The authorised FOI decision-maker records the statutory decision and any applicable review rights.","rows":[["FA1","FOI ss 13, 17–18","Is the request in writing, sufficiently clear to identify the documents, and accompanied by the fee unless waived or reduced? Does another agency hold the document or is its subject matter more closely connected to that agency?","Log the valid request and transfer promptly if s 18 applies. Where multiple bodies hold material, confirm which documents are being sought.","Take reasonable steps to help make the request valid. If the person agrees to informal access, use [policy] and A7."],["FA2","FOI ss 19, 21, 26","Can the requested information be produced as a written document from electronic or other recorded information with equipment ordinarily available? Is an authorised officer managing the clock?","Where s 19 applies, deal with the generated document. Notify as soon as practicable, ordinarily within 30 days of a valid request.","Search for existing documents and document the outcome. Escalate approaching due dates."],["FA3","FOI s 21(2)–(3)","Will actual consultation be undertaken under ss 29, 29A, 31, 31A, 33, 34, or 35, or has the applicant agreed to an extension?","Apply the relevant extension and notify the applicant. Consultation extension is up to 15 days once. Agreed extensions can be up to 30 days each.","Apply the original clock unless another lawful timing provision applies."],["FA4","FOI s 25A","Would processing substantially and unreasonably divert the agency’s resources? Or, is it apparent from the nature of the documents that all are exempt and there is no obligation to give edited copies?","For the resource route, notify and give a reasonable opportunity to consult and narrow before refusal. For the all-exempt route, document why the strict test is met.","Continue the search and apply the [foiex] tests."],["FA5","FOI ss 25, 27 and 33A","Where exemption or irrelevance affects only part, is editing practicable and does the applicant want an edited copy? Have applicable consultation, child notice, review notice, and release-delay conditions cleared?","<b>Must provide</b> the edited copy if s 25 applies. Give reasons and review rights as required. Apply any statutory wait before releasing information about a third party.","If partly or wholly withholding, issue the applicable decision, reasons, and review rights. If a third-party condition is pending, defer the affected access until cleared."]],"note":"For public or informal access, use A7 and the policy branches. A formal FOI disclosure decision authorises the access decided for that request.","sources":[["FOI Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/freedom-information-act-1982/115"],["OVIC timing","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-21/"],["OVIC s 25A","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-25a/"],["OVIC s 25","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-25/"]],"number":15},"foiex":{"category":"FORMAL FOI • EXEMPTION TESTS","title":"Test exemptions for the actual document","intro":"Test the provisions that match the records. A failed exemption test means continue with any other relevant exemption. Apply the edited-copy and review rules at FA5.","rows":[["FX1","ss 28, 29–29B","Is the document a qualifying Cabinet submission, official Cabinet record, draft, ministerial briefing, or otherwise revealing Cabinet deliberation or decision within s 28? For s 29, would disclosure harm Commonwealth/state relations or reveal information communicated in confidence by or for another government, and be contrary to the public interest? For s 29A, is there the specified national security, defence or international-relations harm or confidentiality? For s 29B, is it a Court Services Victoria document relating to a court or VCAT judicial or quasi-judicial function?","Record the exact limb, exception, and required referral or consultation. For Cabinet consider official publication and purely factual material. Use FA5.","Continue to other potentially applicable exemptions."],["FX2","ss 30, 31, 31A","Would disclosure reveal protected deliberative opinion, advice, recommendations, or consultation and be contrary to the public interest (s 30, with factual and other exceptions)? Is there a s 31 enforcement prejudice, source, method, fairness, safety, or qualifying law-enforcement test? Does the document relate to a specified IBAC function (s 31A)?","Match the harm or qualifying function to the actual material. Apply relevant consultation and exceptions, and use FA5.","Continue the exemption assessment."],["FX3","ss 32, 32A–32C","Would the document be privileged from production (s 32)? Would it reveal confidential Treaty-negotiation information (s 32A), protected culturally sensitive or culturally secret material in a Gellung Warl document (s 32B), or specified First Peoples’ Assembly consensus meeting material (s 32C)?","Test privilege and any waiver, or match the precise Treaty document category. Withhold under the applicable exemption and apply FA5.","Consider FX4–FX6."],["FX4","s 33 and s 33A","Would the release unreasonably disclose personal affairs, including identity, address, location, or details from which identity can reasonably be determined? Weigh context and safety, normally protect third-party privacy appropriately, and consider the applicant’s own-information rule and family-violence or child-safety exceptions.","Apply s 33 only if unreasonable. Consult where required and appropriate, use child notice rule if relevant, and clear any notice or review hold before release.","Continue to other exemptions."],["FX5","ss 34–35","Would release reveal trade secrets or other business, commercial, or financial material with the applicable unreasonable disadvantage or agency commercial prejudice? Was information communicated in confidence and does the specific s 35 deliberative or future-supply/public-interest test apply?","Document the limb and likely harm. Consult as required under ss 34–35, subject to exceptions, then apply FA5.","Continue to FX6."],["FX6","ss 36–38","Would release meet s 36 because premature release would likely substantially harm Victoria’s economy or because it would reveal specified negotiating or similar instructions, contrary to the public interest; does the document meet a listed companies/securities category in s 37; or does an in-force enactment specifically prohibit disclosure of that kind of information by the relevant persons under s 38?","Record the actual order, category, or secrecy provision and its scope. Apply FA5.","If no applicable exclusion or exemption remains, grant access in accordance with the Act."]],"note":"Threshold cases. If an unusual exemption, intergovernmental confidence, statutory secrecy, security, cultural confidentiality, or a court restriction remains unresolved, refer through the authorised FOI decision-maker and preserve the clock.","sources":[["Current FOI Act, Part IV","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/freedom-information-act-1982/115"],["OVIC exemption guidance","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/"],["OVIC decision and consultation timing","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/freedom-of-information/foi-guidelines/section-21/"]],"number":16},"policy":{"category":"GOVERNMENT POLICY • DATA SHARING AND PUBLICATION","title":"Apply the policy expectation to share","intro":"A policy can set a duty to respond or a default to publish. Apply it to the proposed lawful release. Document any legal, safety, ethics, licence, or other applicable restriction.","rows":[["G1","VPS Data Sharing Policy • eligibility","Is the proposed recipient within the Victorian Public Sector Data Sharing Policy? Is the request for demonstrated policy making, service planning or delivery need with a clear public benefit? Ensure the data is not restricted under the VDS Act definition.","Apply G2–G3. DFFH is a signatory to the Heads of Agreement.","Use another applicable authority or policy."],["G2","VPS Data Sharing Policy • test grounds","Can the data be shared lawfully and safely, without prejudicing proceedings, endangering a person, infringing rights, or leaving unacceptable ethics, social licence, or other risk? Check safe people, projects, settings, data and outputs. Is a lower-risk version sufficient?","Use best endeavours to share the approved version within a reasonable time. Record any agreed safeguards.","Give the applicable refusal or explain the limits. Consider an available equivalent version or data source."],["G3","VPS Data Sharing Policy • formal request","Has an eligible agency expressly made a formal request under the policy, explained the purpose and public benefit, and described safe holding and use?","Within <b>14 days</b>, supply the lawful data or give written reasons for refusal. Copy a refusal to the Secretary, Department of Government Services.","Handle an ordinary request promptly. If it is a CDO statutory notice, use [vds] and its different clock."],["G4","DataVic Access Policy • open data","Does the State own or have adequate rights over this dataset? Is release lawful and suitable for public access after assessing privacy, re-identification, judicial or other restrictions, security, safety, public health, and existing contracts?","Prepare open, reusable, machine-readable data with suitable licence, metadata, and an accountable custodian. Prioritise high-value data.","Document the restriction. Consider safe aggregation, public metadata where appropriate, or controlled sharing."],["G5","Other publication duties","Is this a financial reporting item, procurement contract, or information routinely published by DFFH?","Use [reporting] for the exact publication or access requirement.","For informal public access, use A7 and [controls]."]],"note":"For an aggregate CSA transfer, decide the agency-to-agency request here if eligible. Apply the public release test again if a later publication is proposed.","sources":[["VPS Data Sharing Policy","https://www.vic.gov.au/victorian-public-sector-data-sharing-policy"],["DFFH signatory","https://www.vic.gov.au/victorian-public-sector-data-sharing-heads-agreement"],["DataVic Access Policy","https://www.data.vic.gov.au/datavic-access-policy"]],"number":17},"reporting":{"category":"GOVERNMENT POLICY • CORPORATE DISCLOSURE","title":"Publish or provide corporate information","intro":"Distinguish open data from formal reporting. Record the responsible area, prescribed fields, deadline, channel, and any narrow redactions before publication.","rows":[["G6","VGPB goods and services contracts","Is it a covered contract, excluding purchases under head agreements where the policy exception applies, with estimated value at or above $100,000 including GST? Does estimated value exceed $10 million including GST?","Publish key details within <b>60 days</b> of award on the central facility. Above $10 million disclose full contract information subject to lawful exclusions, and apply FRD 12 annual report disclosure. Record material variations and applicable redactions.","Check special purchase structures and G7 for construction. Otherwise use another publication ground."],["G7","Construction Instruction 5.2 and FRD 12B","Is it a covered Works or Construction Services contract of at least $100,000 including GST, or above $10 million including GST? Can the Agency publish third-party content?","Publish key details within <b>60 days</b>. Above $10 million apply full-disclosure and annual reporting rules, subject to prescribed exceptions. Where rights are missing, apply the approved inspection or partial-publication process.","Check the goods and services or other publication branch."],["G8","Reporting directions and DFFH practice","Does the item fall in prescribed annual reporting disclosures or DFFH’s published list of additional information available on request, such as major external reviews, fee changes, or consultancy details?","Publish via the required annual reporting process, or provide on request through Corporate Reporting, subject to the applicable FOI rules.","Check G9 or the usual access and release tests."],["G9","FOI ss 7–8 and 16","Does the item fall in the required public statements about functions, records, access, and contacts (s 7), qualifying operational rules or manuals made available as required (s 8), or a proactive or informal release proper under s 16?","Publish or make available through the applicable channel. For proactive or informal access clear the source restriction, privacy, and rights checks on [controls].","Withhold or redesign the proposed public release. A person can still use formal access where applicable."]],"note":"Financial directions and procurement policies may prescribe forms and processes that the responsible business area operates. Keep the legal permission or duty, policy obligation, and approved version in the decision record.","sources":[["VGPB policy","https://www.buyingfor.vic.gov.au/contract-management-and-contract-disclosure-goods-and-services-policy"],["Construction Instruction 5.2","https://www.dtf.vic.gov.au/publishing-details-procurement-undertaken-direction-and-instruction-52"],["Financial reporting directions","https://www.dtf.vic.gov.au/financial-reporting-directions-and-guidance"],["DFFH annual reporting","https://www.dffh.vic.gov.au/publications/annual-reports"],["FOI Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/freedom-information-act-1982/115"]],"number":18},"transfers":{"category":"FINAL RELEASE • TRANSFER AND THIRD PARTIES","title":"Check transfer, identifiers, and recipient controls","intro":"Apply these conditions even if a use or disclosure ground has already passed. Document where the recipient, hosting, backups, administrators, and onward support are located.","rows":[["T1","IPP 9.1 and HPP 9.1 • trigger","Is the release a transfer of personal or health information to someone outside Victoria other than DFFH or the individual? Include contractors and access from another jurisdiction where the test is met.","Establish a ground under T2 or T3 before transfer.","Record why the cross-border rule is inapplicable. Use T4."],["T2","IPP/HPP 9.1(a)–(f)","Does at least one apply? (a) reasonable belief in substantially similar protections under a binding law, scheme, or contract; (b) consent to transfer; (c) necessity for a contract with the person or requested precontractual steps; (d) necessity for a third-party contract in the person’s interest; (e) individual benefit, consent impracticable, and likely consent; or (f) reasonable steps to prevent inconsistent handling by the recipient.","Record which ground and evidence, including contract or practical safeguards where relevant. Use T4.","For health information consider T3. Otherwise hold or redesign the transfer."],["T3","HPP 9.1(g) • other law","For health information, does a separate law actually authorise or require the outside-Victoria transfer?","Document the exact law, recipient, and scope. Use T4.","Hold or redesign."],["T4","IPP 7.3 and HPP 7.3 • identifiers","Does this include a unique identifier assigned by another organisation? If personal, is disclosure necessary to fulfil obligations to the assigner, within IPP 2.1(d)–(g), or consented to? If health, does HPP 7.3 permit the disclosure because it is required for an HPP 2.2(c)–(l) purpose, consented to, or made to the public sector organisation that assigned it?","Retain identifiers only as permitted and if needed. Use T5.","Remove identifiers or hold if an identifier cannot lawfully be supplied. If no such identifier is present use T5."],["T5","PDP Act s 17 • contracted services","Is an external provider acting under a State contract? Do the contract and controls cover binding privacy duties where intended, onward access, data location, security, retention, incident handling, return, and destruction?","Confirm who remains accountable and document the conditions. Finish [controls].","If contractual conditions are missing resolve them before discretionary transfer. When there is no contractor continue [controls]."]],"note":"Public publication, secure single-recipient transfers, contractor processing, and recipient linkage have different risk profiles. Approve only the version and use assessed.","sources":[["PDP Act, Schedule 1","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/privacy-and-data-protection-act-2014/034"],["Health Records Act, Schedule 1","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/health-records-act-2001/050"],["OVIC transborder guidance","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/book/ipp-9-transborder-data-flows/"]],"number":19},"controls":{"number":20,"category":"FINAL RELEASE DECISION","title":"Can the approved version leave DFFH?","intro":"Apply these checks proportionately alongside the requirements of the chosen pathway. Resolve unclear conditions promptly, especially where a statutory deadline or safety risk applies.","rows":[["R1","Exact authority and scope","Have you identified the precise duty, power, privacy ground, or lawful basis for releasing non-personal material in the departmental function? Does it cover this recipient, purpose, data, and use?","Record whether the outcome is <b>may disclose</b> or <b>must disclose</b>. Move to R2.","Stop discretionary release. For a possible duty, get a prompt determination from the responsible decision-maker."],["R2","PDP Act s 3, HRA s 3, IPP/HPP 7","Has the proposed version passed either the relevant test for identifiable information (including IPP/HPP 7 where relevant) or the re-identification assessment? For the latter, consider small counts, linkage keys, rare combinations, free text, timing, location, and other data available to the recipient.","Record the assessment or the applicable ground and identifier conditions. Move to R3.","Treat reasonably identifiable material under the relevant privacy pathway, or reduce it lawfully and retest."],["R3","IPP/HPP 9.1, PDP Act s 17","If an external recipient outside Victoria can access the information, does a specific IPP or HPP 9.1 ground apply? If outsourcing, have applicable privacy obligations been addressed in the contract? Include hosting and remote support in this assessment.","Apply [transfers] as relevant. Record the ground or why it is inapplicable. Move to R4.","Hold the transfer. Confirm jurisdiction, recipient and binding safeguards, or redesign."],["R4","Charter ss 13, 38 and security","Has the public authority properly considered relevant rights and compatibility with them, including privacy? Are protections in place under IPP 4.1/HPP 4.1 and PDP Act Part 4 or Part 5/VPDSS as applicable? Check minimum necessary scope, access, and secure delivery.","Move to R5.","Resolve the rights or security issue with the relevant decision-maker."],["R5","Approval and recordkeeping","Is the correct delegate or statutory officer approving the exact version? Is there a record of source, purpose, recipient, section and facts, approvals, delivery, onward use, retention or disposal, and any scheme-specific notices or logs?","Use [record], then release within the approved scope. Retain the decision and evidence.","Resolve missing approval or evidence. Document any refusal, reduced scope, or delay as the applicable law requires."]],"note":"A recipient agreement can establish access, retention, and onward-use controls. Record the legal basis independently. Reassess a new recipient, new linkage, new purpose, or publication of the shared information.","sources":[["Charter","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/charter-human-rights-and-responsibilities-act-2006"],["PDP Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/privacy-and-data-protection-act-2014/034"],["Health Records Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/health-records-act-2001/050"],["VPDSS","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/information-security/standards/"],["Public Records Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/public-records-act-1973"],["OVIC de-identification guide","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/privacy/resources-for-organisations/an-introduction-to-de-identification/"]]},"record":{"category":"DECISION AND EVIDENCE","title":"Record a release, refusal, or referral","intro":"Use the applicable outcome below. Record the source, version, precise recipient, legal or policy route, findings, conditions, delegate, and relevant deadlines.","rows":[["D1","Must disclose","Has a statutory duty, binding instrument, access right, scheme obligation, or other mandatory disclosure been established for this exact version and recipient?","Release the required scope in the prescribed manner. Log the deadline, authority, reasons for any excluded portion, conditions, and delivery evidence.","Use D2. A duty to respond can still allow refusal on specified grounds."],["D2","May disclose or policy favours release","Is lawful permission established and are source, privacy, Charter, recipient and security checks complete? Is the required decision-maker satisfied with the version and conditions?","Approve and release, or document a legitimate reason to decline the discretionary release. Record any policy publication deadline or response requirement.","Use D3 or D4."],["D3","Withhold or release a narrower version","Has a prohibition, failed required test, or other ground been established for some or all of the release?","Withhold those fields or that version. Reassess a lawfully redacted or aggregated alternative. Give reasons and review information where the applicable process requires them.","Use D4 if the problem is unresolved facts or authority."],["D4","Hold and refer for a decision","Is an essential fact, source-specific condition, case instrument, or delegation unverified? Is there uncertainty about conflicts between legal rules, privileged material, or urgent safety?","Refer promptly to the accountable delegate or specialist channel. Provide the precise issue, scope, and due date. Record what must be confirmed before release.","Return to D1–D3 with the established findings."],["D5","Reassess a changed release","Has the recipient, purpose, audience, version, linkage, onward use, or handling changed since approval?","Run the affected tests again and obtain approval for the new scope.","Keep the decision and evidence in the official record under applicable recordkeeping rules."]],"note":"A legal decision on an actual release can require the text of an order, a contract condition, or a verified delegation. This guide supplies the decision path and the evidence to obtain for those cases.","sources":[["Public Records Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/public-records-act-1973"],["OVIC sharing guidance","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/privacy/resources-for-organisations/information-sharing-and-privacy/"]],"number":21},"csa":{"title":"Sharing a statistical extract with the CSA","intro":"Worked example. Apply the tree to the exact information proposed for transfer, then assess later public release separately.","note":"<b>Example decision record.</b><br/><b>Evidence.</b> The proposed output is an aggregate count table. The source owner has cleared the scope. Small or distinctive cells were combined after assessing linkage and other information available to the CSA.<br/><b>Decision.</b> The delegate may approve the specific table for the stated statistical purpose if the source and privacy findings are evidenced and the remaining release checks pass. Record version, recipient, purpose, and safeguards.<br/><b>Published example.</b> DataVic describes a historical DHHS transfer of de-identified IRIS data to the CSA for the Family Violence Database. The current disclosure must be assessed on its own facts.","sources":[["Crime Statistics Act","https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/in-force/acts/crime-statistics-act-2014/004"],["Historical IRIS release","https://discover.data.vic.gov.au/dataset/family-violence-database-interated-reports-and-information-system-data-tables"],["OVIC de-identification","https://ovic.vic.gov.au/privacy/resources-for-organisations/an-introduction-to-de-identification/"]],"rows":[["CSA1","Recipient and purpose","Is the request for statistical analysis within the Chief Statistician’s functions in s 5 of the Crime Statistics Act 2014? Sections 7 and 7A set out access powers for police and applicable court data.","Record the CSA purpose, then identify DFFH’s own lawful basis. Go to CSA2.","Clarify the purpose or consider any other genuine authority."],["CSA2","Source law and scope","Can DFFH confirm it may share statistics for this purpose and that no source secrecy, suppression, or binding use restriction applies to this extract? Consider any program-specific law and upstream dataset conditions.","Go to CSA3. Keep evidence of the source and cleared scope.","Resolve the source restriction or redesign the outputs."],["CSA3","PDP Act s 3 and HRA s 3","Can the CSA reasonably identify an individual from the fields, combinations, linkage keys, and other data available to it?","Use CSA4 for identifiable records. Masking names alone is insufficient.","If otherwise permitted, apply [policy] and [controls] to the non-identifying extract."],["CSA4","IPP 2.1(c), HPP 2.2(g), or VDS Act","For the proposed identifiable statistics or linkage, does the relevant research ground meet every element on [ipp] or [hpp]? If an integration route is proposed, does the specific recipient qualify and do [vds] ss 5 and 15 apply?","Document the chosen legal pathway and restrictions. Apply [controls].","Hold the identifiable extract. Consider lawfully aggregated statistics or another verified pathway."],["CSA5","Separate public release","If a party will publish, has it reassessed the exact output for the public audience, with all applicable restrictions, including VDS Act s 19 if relevant?","Record and approve the public release under the applicable pathway.","Keep approval limited to the authorised transfer."]]}}};
